  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to data. It was introduced by Alex with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The team expanded in September with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. In July, Emily called for R&D proposals to leverage AI for data visualization. The budget was later adjusted to $550,000 by Jordan to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration, while Carla noted a $55,000 budget increase for the compliance plan. Neil reported a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two, with a detailed update scheduled for November 20th. The project launch date is set for March 15, 2024. Additionally, security protocols were updated for multi-factor authentication and encryption effective January next year, and discussions are underway for a potential partnership with TechInnovate to leverage their AI technology."
